RESIDUE3 C8 — Win32: the dynamic-scale loader, live FAIL-CLEAN receipts, DOOM D7
================================================================================

What this patch carries
-----------------------
The *receipt half* of RESIDUE3_PLAN.md §C8 (boxes 2 – 5):

  * the two live guest fixtures that turn RES-57's 820 `static-only` pairs and
    RES-58's 35 FAIL-CLEAN functions from source-level claims into measured
    answers (`w32/tests/w32c8_static_slice.c`, `w32/tests/w32c8_failclean.c`,
    `tools/w32_static_slice.py`, and their gates);
  * the gap ledger that learned to NAME symbols instead of counting them
    (`w32_gap_at()`, 128 names, and `w32run` printing one line per miss);
  * the two bug fixes the measurement found: `LoadLibraryA` answering NULL for
    `imm32`/`ole32`/`uxtheme`, and `ERROR_NO_SUCH_PRIVILEGE` defined as 1530
    where Windows defines 1313 — including the W32A-9 gate that had been
    pinning the wrong constant in place;
  * DOOM_PLAN D7: the Win32 engine build, the 52 named gaps, and the recorded
    implement/refuse decisions.

22 files (16 modified, 6 new).  `git apply --check` clean; a full replay
reproduces every file byte-for-byte.

Why the loader half is not in here
----------------------------------
C8 box 1 (the streaming relocation path, the 256/128/32 module table, the gap
API core) was written in an earlier session on a sandbox that does not persist
`/tmp` and carries no git history, so its pre-image no longer exists in this
environment and a faithful diff of it cannot be cut.  It is pinned by hash in
`RESIDUE3_C8_receipts.manifest` instead, and its receipts live in
`w32/app_ledger/audacity-3.7.5.gap` § "C8: WALL 1 IS CLOSED".

Baseline note
-------------
This tree is not a git repository and the phase's pre-image was reconstructed
by script (this continuation's edits reversed by exact string).  The plan-doc
hunks therefore read from that reconstruction: the C8 section's five boxes were
un-flipped and their "Landed/Done 2026-11-05" notes removed to form it.


